{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01R5", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nX_1 \\ar[d] \\ar[r]_{f_1} & Y_1 \\ar[d] \\\\\nX_2 \\ar[r]^{f_2} & Y_2\n}\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$Z_i \\subset Y_i$", "MATH_0003": "$i = 1, 2$", "MATH_0004": "$f_i$", "MATH_0005": "$Y_1 \\to Y_2$", "MATH_0006": "$Z_1 \\to Z_2$", "MATH_0007": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nX_1 \\ar[r] \\ar[d] & Z_1 \\ar[d] \\ar[r] & Y_1 \\ar[d] \\\\\nX_2 \\ar[r] & Z_2 \\ar[r] & Y_2\n}\n$$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-factor-factor}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7d722639477eae1f5b38e2bc1226093f81a80763673d337a67f7ca9d31c1a012", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2b1a0ba8aeda3e73e6f0899ae25ba7c50de7d451d80e17cc1b41f0b9210dc0d4", "source_text": "Let\n<MATH_0001>\nbe a commutative diagram of schemes. Let <MATH_0002>, <MATH_0003> be\nthe scheme theoretic image of <MATH_0004>. Then the morphism\n<MATH_0005> induces a morphism <MATH_0006> and a\ncommutative diagram\n<MATH_0007>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a4f0037d18d892d2874f028708f183cba96caaac118b7d5d70d2314e0b5abdcb", "unit_id": "tag:01R9:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01R5", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$Z_2$", "MATH_0002": "$Y_1$", "MATH_0003": "$Y_1$", "MATH_0004": "$f_1$", "MATH_0005": "$Z_1$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a3514d853e265abf33c920ef8c6e0df3132ee2b019f04be7b17963e651207162", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6aa28fa722277f6976ad7bf1efa0211948bfd0b22106d01c33d69ae1b0fa0ed6", "source_text": "The scheme theoretic inverse image of <MATH_0001> in <MATH_0002>\nis a closed subscheme of <MATH_0003> through\nwhich <MATH_0004> factors. Hence <MATH_0005> is contained in this.\nThis proves the lemma.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0fc0c4068282ea87ed8ff05b34b16b66ac4d7657aa8b015533b0ca5b13b4dba4", "unit_id": "tag:01R9:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01R5", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$\\overline{f(X)}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-scheme-theoretic-image-reduced}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:95e5aded83ae0322a25977815752ecb8497214e187eb1cfc04f5e5290730f9c2", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c2b7a3c4aa65a30572cb35ae8470bc6ca4041354644fc5203c7780f0bd0ddbc7", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\nIf <MATH_0002> is reduced, then the scheme theoretic image of <MATH_0003> is\nthe reduced induced scheme structure on <MATH_0004>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:85a4413645db87a72b9b69404552c7e465c37069a5299b794efe9355841d9f8f", "unit_id": "tag:056B:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01R5", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\overline{f(X)}$", "MATH_0002": "$Y$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-map-into-reduction}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:03beadcf664b118e148a15d206379c77897fdf627317def384f1fd0a7e071ee6", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:24e3c5964b5273ce794a576d5813af866e7e5680c20ff596094b0581d453847c", "source_text": "This is true because the reduced induced scheme structure on <MATH_0001>\nis clearly the smallest closed subscheme of <MATH_0002> through which <MATH_0003> factors,\nsee\nSchemes, Lemma <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:80252b87dfdb6a9fda856cd86c29b476c74c922a02afcc3bd9871ea857c685e4", "unit_id": "tag:056B:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01R5", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$V \\subset Y$", "MATH_0003": "$s : V \\to X$", "MATH_0004": "$f \\circ s = \\text{id}_V$", "MATH_0005": "$Y'$", "MATH_0006": "$s$", "MATH_0007": "$Y' \\to Y$", "MATH_0008": "$V$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-scheme-theoretic-image-of-partial-section}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d3855049bdeddecec61899e5c6ccf533ffd4d6a4e7e85163f5a9c304759a039c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e0a1d0ed8455e21bd9bf117e9a4cf630d91c022e3612836c9bafd79bb8a01010", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a separated morphism of schemes.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a retrocompact open. Let <MATH_0003>\nbe a morphism such that <MATH_0004>.\nLet <MATH_0005> be the scheme theoretic image of <MATH_0006>.\nThen <MATH_0007> is an isomorphism over <MATH_0008>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2bee93493e4aaf3d32c87c3b95942b6fe6daa488a7a190954d9885938a2a14b7", "unit_id": "tag:0CNG:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01R5", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$V$", "MATH_0002": "$Y$", "MATH_0003": "$V \\to Y$", "MATH_0004": "$s : V \\to X$", "MATH_0005": "$Y'$", "MATH_0006": "$s$", "MATH_0007": "$Y' \\cap f^{-1}(V)$", "MATH_0008": "$f^{-1}(V) \\to V$", "MATH_0009": "$Y' \\cap f^{-1}(V) \\to V$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{topology-definition-quasi-compact}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-quasi-compact-permanence}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-quasi-compact-scheme-theoretic-image}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-section-immersion}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a1dfda039b764e7f88e9cce23e794841aa517af0f5e91e7a16d35004902a104a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:01177b3c7e001de2f32efbf062d21cf49746f76d57a115eaa84e307b1f7dea83", "source_text": "The assumption that <MATH_0001> is retrocompact in <MATH_0002>\n(Topology, Definition <REF_0001>)\nmeans that <MATH_0003> is a quasi-compact morphism.\nBy Schemes, Lemma <REF_0002>\nthe morphism <MATH_0004> is quasi-compact.\nHence the construction of the scheme theoretic image <MATH_0005>\nof <MATH_0006> commutes with restriction to opens by\nLemma <REF_0003>.\nIn particular, we see that <MATH_0007> is the\nscheme theoretic image of a section of the separated\nmorphism <MATH_0008>. Since a section of a separated\nmorphism is a closed immersion\n(Schemes, Lemma <REF_0004>),\nwe conclude that\n<MATH_0009> is an isomorphism as desired.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0d7c8a2c63dd05bacc01056c407511839fcdf613643952666140b4d8d6090d7b", "unit_id": "tag:0CNG:proof"}
